# No password for sudo.
#
# The account's password is not a meaningful control here: sshd is key-only, so
# anyone typing this already holds the private key, and re-typing a password
# behind that adds friction rather than security.
#
# It does mean the password protects exactly one thing — console login at the
# physical machine, with root locked — which is the recovery path when SSH and
# Tailscale are both unavailable. 03-chroot.sh sets and verifies it for that
# reason.
%wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
